      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "On #123842, I'd have expected the \"Google testing\" check to run, but I don't see it anywhere in the list of checks.\r\n\r\n* It's had plenty of time to start; the last update to the PR was over 2 hours ago.\r\n* It's [documented](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/wiki/Understanding-google-testing) to start when a Flutter hacker approves the PR.\r\n\r\n  The PR's author (me) is a Flutter hacker, so I'd expect that to count, just like it counts toward the two approvals required by the autosubmit bot. And I think I've seen that working on other PRs.\r\n\r\nIs this intended behavior in some way? Or is there a bug or an operational issue?\r\n\r\nPossible related issues:\r\n* Sometimes the check does appear, but stays in \"Pending\" status indefinitely: #123289\r\n* Other issues linked to from that one.\r\n",
